title: The Word of God – Inspired, Preserved, Understood
description: The King James Bible, the preservation of scripture, scripture alone over tradition, rightly dividing the word, and Christ in all the scriptures, from the teachings on the Word of God.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-scripture.html
highlight: word

# One deck for the whole of studies/data/topics/scripture.json, each theme given the same weight.
# Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed. The verses the teachings typed out are shown from the KJV.
# Fixed: "it is a hole" -> "a whole" (8568), "them that out their trust" -> "put" (17410),
# "Standfast" -> "Stand fast" (7020).

=== Introduction
--- The Word of God [title]
overline: Doctrine · The Word of God
heading: Thy Word Is Settled in Heaven
sub: The KJV, the preservation of scripture, and rightly dividing it.
refs: Psalm 119:89; Psalm 12:6-7; 2 Timothy 3:16-17; 2 Timothy 2:15
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 14763
--- The Bible is the word of God
big: Psalm 138:2 | mark: thou hast magnified thy word above all thy name
p: Jesus Christ is the word of God. The word of God created all things. The word of God is what we place our hope on, and are never ashamed. The word of God is the lamp to our feet, our shield, our strength and our sword.
p: The word of God is found in the collection of inspired scripture, 66 books known collectively as the Bible. Not paper and cardstock, ink and glue. But the words and their spirit and the truth.
refs: John 1:1; John 1:14; Revelation 19:13

# from 6003, 12902
--- One voice in all of scripture
lead: It is all one word, one testimony, one book made up of 66 smaller books, written over thousands of years, but with one voice, the inspiration of God, through the Spirit, testifying of the Son.
p: Whether it is Moses, the prophets, the apostles... Christ Himself, all of it has a consistent and clear voice. Not a collection of the works of men, but the word of an eternal and living God.
p: Nothing in God's word is coincidental, incidental or accidental. If God repeats something, it is for emphasis and our edification.

=== Every word of God is pure
# from 17410
--- Every word of God is pure
kicker: Every word of God is pure
big: Proverbs 30:5-6 | mark: Every word of God is pure; Add thou not unto his words
p: Verses 5 and 6 give the inspired case for Biblical fundamentalism. And if every word of God is pure, we need an “every word” Bible. We are blessed that we have one, in the Authorized version, in English. Preserved by God unto all generations.

# from 9104, 17148
--- By every word
kicker: Every word of God is pure
big: Matthew 4:4 | mark: by every word that proceedeth out of the mouth of God
p: When Satan tempted Him with rewards of the flesh, twisting scripture to do it, Jesus cites the word to both rebuke the devil and keep Himself pure. It's Jesus' first lesson to us. We live by His word.
p: It was good enough for Jesus in the desert against Satan. It is good enough for us today who follow Him.

# from 6499, 5433
--- Yea, hath God said?
kicker: Every word of God is pure
scripture: Genesis 3:1 | mark: Yea, hath God said
lead: “Yea, hath God said?” This is Satan's oldest trick. Casting doubt upon God's word to get us to sin. This is the reason for false Bible versions. This is the way of false prophets.
p: “Many of the earliest manuscripts leave this passage out... the Greek here could actually mean this instead... You need a seminary graduate to understand the Bible!” Fill in your own example of “Yea, hath God said..?” here.
p: For where there is doubt or uncertainty, there is no power.

# from 6591, 14102
--- These things happened
kicker: Every word of God is pure
big: 1 Corinthians 10:11 | mark: all these things happened unto them for ensamples
p: The Spirit tells us that these things **happened**, and for a reason; as examples and admonition for us. We can know that these aren't merely stories and folklore, but actual events.
p: We could go into the fossils of sealife found on top of Everest, or deposits of salt in high plateaus. But the Bible says it's true, and that's enough.

# from 12896, 13024
--- Ye shall not add unto the word
kicker: Every word of God is pure
scripture: Deuteronomy 4:2 | mark: Ye shall not add unto the word which I command you, neither shall ye diminish ought from it
p: The recording of the law begins and ends with the same admonition. Yet so many today will cling to false versions of God's word that remove and add to it.
p: It is the opposite of mystery religions and gnosticism. All of the information is given up front and the means to understand provided even the lowliest babe in Christ. We just have to read it for ourselves.
refs: Deuteronomy 12:32; Revelation 22:18-19
