=== The preservation of God's word
# from 17708, 7597
--- Thou shalt preserve them
kicker: The preservation of God's word
big: Psalm 12:6-7 | mark: purified seven times; thou shalt preserve them from this generation for ever
p: If man needs every word of God to live, as much as bread, man needs access to every word He has given us. The blessing of having a consolidated, complete, incorruptible source, an every-word Bible, cannot be overstated.
p: The 6 earlier English attempts, like a refiner's fire. We have the purified silver of the Authorized version.

# from 12090
--- The burned scroll written again
kicker: The preservation of God's word
p: In **Jeremiah 36**, when the king heard the word of the Lord, he cut up the scroll and cast it into the fire. And God said to write the words again in another scroll, the scripture not being hid, impossible to destroy.
p: Because the word of God is spirit and life, not the paper it is confined to, but the truth that is from everlasting to everlasting.
big: Matthew 24:35 | mark: my words shall not pass away
refs: Jeremiah 36:23; Jeremiah 36:28; Isaiah 40:8

# from 4519, 14987, 15005
--- One jot or one tittle
kicker: The preservation of God's word
big: Matthew 5:18 | mark: one jot or one tittle shall in no wise pass from the law
p: Jesus and the Apostles quoted the OT from the Hebrew texts, compiled by Levite scribes. Jots and tittles are explicitly terms from the Hebrew alphabet and written Hebrew.
p: William Tyndale translated and published, in 1526, the first-ever mechanically-printed New Testament in the English language. More than 90 percent of the King James Version that was published nearly 100 years later matched Tyndale's. He was strangled and then burned at the stake for translating the Bible into English.

# from 2657, 16368, 17709, 727
--- What the modern versions change
kicker: The preservation of God's word
lead: The first thing modern versions do is create doubt and deny the preservation of the inspired word.
table: Verse | The King James | The modern versions
tr: [[Acts 8:37]] | *I believe that Jesus Christ is the Son of God.* | Removed or footnoted into doubt
tr: [[1 Corinthians 1:18]] | *unto us which are saved* | “to us who are being saved”
tr: [[Psalm 12:7]] | *thou shalt preserve them* | “you will guard us”
tr: [[1 Timothy 6:10]] | *the root of all evil* | “all kinds of evil”
p: The KJV's “are saved” perfectly preserves the assured, completed state implied by the Greek, whereas “are being saved” turns that blessed assurance into a continuous, unfinished process, sowing doubt.

# from 8332, 8288, 16076
--- The content, not the container
kicker: The preservation of God's word
lead: I am King James only because it is the perfect and preserved word of God in English. My native tongue. What a blessing that is. But what is important is the content not the container.
p: To say the KJV was itself a separate inspiration, given to the translators, implies that God's word hadn't been preserved for all ages, but only in 1611 became perfect. This makes the translation itself an idol.
p: It would deny preservation to say that the word of God was not preserved until 1611, as millions were saved from every nation and tongue long before it, by faith. The power is in the word itself, and the Spirit moving in those receiving it. Not in the languages.
read: app:doctrine-scripture~17708 | Pure words preserved for ever
read: app:doctrine-scripture~12090 | The burned scroll written again
read: app:doctrine-scripture~16368 | Are saved versus are being saved
read: app:doctrine-scripture~8332 | Making an idol of the translation

=== Scripture alone, not tradition
# from 7030
--- Of none effect through your tradition
kicker: Scripture alone, not tradition
scripture: Mark 7:7-9 | mark: teaching for doctrines the commandments of men; that ye may keep your own tradition
p: Making the word of God, which is scripture, *of none effect through your tradition*. This applies to ANY extra-scriptural doctrines and traditions that contradict the word of God.
take: Any tradition of man that contradicts scripture is heresy. Period.

# from 7031
--- They searched the scriptures daily
kicker: Scripture alone, not tradition
big: Acts 17:11 | mark: searched the scriptures daily, whether those things were so
p: The Apostles and evangelists who went out to preach the word of God and the Gospel taught the doctrine of Christ from scripture. Paul *reasoned with them out of the scriptures* ([[Acts 17:2-3]]).
p: He gave them no instruction or tradition that contradicted scripture, or else how would they search *the scriptures daily, whether those things were so?*

# from 7018, 7020, 13251
--- Hold the traditions
kicker: Scripture alone, not tradition
big: 2 Thessalonians 2:15 | mark: hold the traditions which ye have been taught, whether by word, or our epistle
p: Paul is writing to the independent NT church in Thessalonica with a specific message regarding a specific topic; End times prophecy. We don't have to guess at what mystery doctrines were being given by these “traditions.” Paul tells us in the second verse.
p: *Stand fast*, whether you learned this Biblical doctrine through preaching by an Apostle, taken from scripture and the words of Christ, or by epistles. Amen! And when Paul writes of tradition again ([[2 Thessalonians 3:6-10]]), he writes what that tradition is.

# from 13249, 13905
--- What is written is sufficient
kicker: Scripture alone, not tradition
scripture: John 20:30-31 | mark: But these are written, that ye might believe
p: That what is written is sufficient to believe on Jesus Christ, the Son of God, and by believing, have life through His name.
p: *And the word of the Lord was precious in those days; there was no open vision.* We are currently in the same state; there is no open vision, and so the word of the Lord should be kept precious. We have His full revelation.
