read: app:doctrine-scripture~7031 | Paul reasoned out of the scriptures
read: app:doctrine-scripture~7020 | The traditions were end-times teaching from scripture
read: app:doctrine-scripture~13249 | What is written is sufficient

=== Rightly dividing the word
# from 10660, 6287
--- Study to shew thyself approved
kicker: Rightly dividing the word
big: 2 Timothy 2:15 | mark: rightly dividing the word of truth
p: We study scripture for God's approval, and to not be ashamed, that is taken astray, caught off guard by an argument we don't have an answer for, being misled by those who wrestle with scripture to pull out false doctrines.
p: And so we gain wisdom and knowledge by studying God's word. Not by endless argument and debate. But by the word of God.

# from 1152, 14353
--- Comparing spiritual things with spiritual
kicker: Rightly dividing the word
big: 1 Corinthians 2:13 | mark: comparing spiritual things with spiritual
p: You can't form doctrine around a verse or two and your assumptions and own reasonings, to fit doctrine you've decided on. You have to let God's word tell you what it means directly. God is not an author of confusion.
p: Like anything else in the Bible, the answer to our confusion is found by comparing scripture with scripture.

# from 5144, 5851, 7040
--- Context tells us what is meant
kicker: Rightly dividing the word
lead: Most instances of the word saved in the Bible refer to rescue of the flesh, not salvation of the soul.
p: Just as “saved” in scripture isn't always referring to justification by faith, “faith” isn't always referring to the saving faith that we need to be redeemed. These are important distinctions, and understanding the context of the terms will save you when some try to cherry pick verses.
p: Unless God or someone in the Spirit speaking for God says it, we have to look at context to see if what a man in scripture is saying is true, or the truth from their perspective, or possibly a lie or rationalization.
refs: Matthew 10:22; Genesis 20:12

# from 3653, 17324, 12533
--- Primary doctrine and pet theories
kicker: Rightly dividing the word
lead: Just because you believe something about the world to be true, doesn't make it Biblical doctrine.
p: Other than the Gospel and a few primary doctrines, there's interpretation of secondary and tertiary doctrine that's open for discussion. Literal creation is a primary doctrine. Biblical age as determined by generations is secondary.
p: No doctrine should stand alone on a parable. The Bible is very clear on doctrine, and things that have to be forced out of the text aren't worthy of being dogmatic.
callout: The Bible is not for our eisegesis to win fights online. Especially about carnal things. It is for the winning of souls.
