=== The Bible can be understood
# from 6318
--- Have ye not read?
kicker: The Bible can be understood
big: Mark 12:10 | mark: have ye not read this scripture
p: God, who is a loving God, just and true, and who readily gives wisdom to all who seek it, doesn't think it unreasonable to say “*Have ye not read this scripture?*” to man.
p: God gave us His word to be understood. He gave us His word that we may know Him. He inspired it, preserved it and sent men of God to preach it, because in His mind He thinks that it is clear and understandable.

# from 16891
--- The word is nigh thee
kicker: The Bible can be understood
scripture: Deuteronomy 30:11-14 | mark: it is not hidden from thee; But the word is very nigh unto thee
p: God's word was there present with them that they could know it. In a similar way, as Paul writes to the Romans quoting Deuteronomy, the Word, which is Christ Jesus, also came down from heaven that we may know God's will.
refs: Romans 10:8-9

# from 3638, 8943
--- Spiritually discerned
kicker: The Bible can be understood
big: 1 Corinthians 2:14 | mark: because they are spiritually discerned
p: The wisdom of God is available to all who believe the Gospel and stay in His word. Christianity is an anti-gnostic religion. The knowledge of who Christ Jesus is and what He did is the great mystery that is told us plainly in the Gospel. It's the entry point for the novice, not some secret kept for the adept.
p: You do not need a third party intermediary to explain to you biblical doctrines. If you struggle understanding the Bible yourself, read it more and pray for wisdom.

# from 10436, 15501, 17639
--- Nothing replaces your own reading
kicker: The Bible can be understood
lead: There is no study guide, commentary, sermon, video, post, meme or any other thing that takes the place of your own reading and guidance of the Spirit to all wisdom and understanding.
p: Those that walk in the Spirit meditate in His word day and night. By doing so, we become as a tree planted by the river, constantly fed and nourished.
p: There are 150 Psalms and 31 chapters of Proverbs. That's 181 chapters. Read through them twice, that's 362 days. (God even gives you 3 days of grace a year!)
big: Psalm 1:2-3 | mark: in his law doth he meditate day and night
read: app:doctrine-scripture~6318 | Have ye not read this scripture?
read: app:doctrine-scripture~16891 | The word is nigh thee
