read: app:doctrine-scripture~15501 | Reading the Bible for yourself

=== Scripture opened in Christ
# from 17987
--- Then opened he their understanding
kicker: Scripture opened in Christ
scripture: Luke 24:44-45 | mark: Then opened he their understanding, that they might understand the scriptures
p: He explicitly references the three divisions of the Old Testament, the Law, the Prophets, and the Psalms, and grants them the ability to finally see past the “dark sayings” to understand the plain truth of the Gospel.
p: The Old Testament scriptures aren't an empty recitation of genealogy, geography and events. They are the words of eternal life, and all these were written to point the way to Jesus.

# from 11480, 17247, 15345
--- Christ is found in every book
kicker: Scripture opened in Christ
lead: Everything points to Him. Jesus is found in every book of the Bible.
p: The faith of the Old Testament saints was the same as New; believing on the Lord to save us, a gift given in grace from our Father because He so loved us.
p: All scripture, given by inspiration, is the word of God, and all scripture, including the Proverbs of Solomon, are the word, and all are about Christ. Christ could be preached to unbelievers through the book of Micah, just as Jesus was preached to the Ethiopian Eunuch by Philip, using Isaiah 53.
refs: Luke 24:27; Acts 8:35; John 5:39

# from 16983, 17703
--- Read it first for Jesus
kicker: Scripture opened in Christ
lead: It is incredibly important when reading scripture to look first at how it applies to Jesus.
p: A lot of people read scripture, to read themselves into the text. To make it about them. God is telling us about God. Almost every heresy imaginable that is drawn from the Bible, comes from people making the focus themselves.
p: When I read and react to the text, all I see is Jesus, the gospel, and the clear and present application of worship in our lives. Meanwhile, many studies become hyper fixated on the context, buried under jargon. Seeking to be wise, they become fools.
big: John 3:30 | mark: He must increase, but I must decrease
read: app:doctrine-scripture~17987 | Dark sayings made plain in Christ
read: app:doctrine-scripture~11480 | Christ is found in every book
