=== The sure word of prophecy
# from 5280
--- A more sure word of prophecy
kicker: The sure word of prophecy
scripture: 2 Peter 1:16-21 | mark: We have also a more sure word of prophecy; holy men of God spake as they were moved by the Holy Ghost
p: Peter writes that even as he witnessed the transfiguration, and heard the voice of God from the heavens, we should know that the testimony of scripture is even more important.

# from 15704, 16017, 16300
--- That ye may know He is the Lord
kicker: The sure word of prophecy
lead: The prophecies of the Bible are so precise, prescient and perfect, that it is impossible to believe anything other than an omniscient God could have made them known.
p: The destruction of Babylon by the Medes in 539BC is foretold by Isaiah in approximately 700BC. Nations that God said would never recover, didn't. Egypt was never a power again. Assyria was gone. Babylon never rebuilt.
p: And then, knowing this, how can you hear the promises of God in Christ, eternal life, the resurrection of the dead and His everlasting Kingdom and not trust that they are true?
refs: Isaiah 13:17-19; Daniel 2:44; Romans 10:17
read: app:doctrine-scripture~5280 | The transfiguration and a more sure word
read: app:doctrine-scripture~16017 | Prophecy proves an omniscient God

=== Built upon a rock
# from 10637, 2376
--- Built upon a rock [title]
overline: The Word of God
heading: Built upon a Rock
big: Matthew 7:24-25 | mark: which built his house upon a rock
center: Basing your faith on the unchanging and preserved word of God is building on rock. Everything else is sand.
center: Perfect. Inspired. Preserved. True.
